  "scope": "Shared single-start preparation preserves ordinary chat/plan/agent behavior. A comparison reserves all replies, revalidates current history inside one atomic transaction, persists complete group/context/user/assistant records once, then announces one full state and opens all streams. Group-start write failure preserves both complete files and unrelated active runs; retry is intact, and queued shutdown releases all reservations before any request. Individual provider failure/stop and the original 30/10-second native conditions remain. Actual 84 MB/297-thread local startup benchmark and six native comparison checks pass; local benchmark uses a held mock gateway and does not measure hosted HTTP/IPC deadline contributions. Complete current native/source, matching distribution, hosted acceptance and the remaining full capability/UI scope are pending."
